.docname {Developer Guide}
.include {docs}

Welcome to the **Ambitwin Developer Guide**. Ambitwin is a real-time crowd monitoring platform built on a digital twin: it streams live IoT sensor data into a 3D model of each building, for the people who manage those facilities.

.box {Core paradigm} type:{note}
    Every service owns one bounded context and its own database. Services talk through their APIs and broker events, so telemetry, the twin and alerts can each change on their own.

## System Capabilities

.mindmap center:{Ambitwin}
    - [Digital Twin](../docs/domain-model/domain-buildings.qd)
        - 3D spatial building model
    - [Telemetry Ingestion](../docs/domain-model/domain-ingestion.qd)
        - Sensor readings, thresholds
    - [Telemetry Distribution](../docs/domain-model/domain-distribution.qd)
        - Per-building live streams
    - [Alerting & Safety](../docs/domain-model/domain-alerting.qd)
        - Threshold breaches, Web Push
    - [Identity & Access](../docs/domain-model/domain-identity.qd)
        - OIDC, memberships, Cedar
    - [Knowledge Assistant](../docs/domain-model/domain-assistance.qd)
        - RAG over this guide
    - [Simulators](../docs/setup/sensor-simulator.qd)
        - Synthetic telemetry

## Domain Responsibilities

Each bounded context runs on its own and exchanges events with the others.

.cards
    .card title:{Telemetry Ingestion} footer:{.tag {Rust + Kafka} variant:{good}}
        Takes one batch per building tick, checks thresholds and publishes raw readings.

    .card title:{Digital Twin} footer:{.tag {Rust + MongoDB} variant:{good}}
        Holds the spatial model of each building and estimates Wi-Fi device positions.

    .card title:{Alerting} footer:{.tag {Rust + Redis} variant:{good}}
        Consumes threshold breaches, dedupes them on a cooldown and delivers Web Push.

    .card title:{Identity & Tenancy} footer:{.tag {Go + Cedar} variant:{good}}
        Exchanges Keycloak tokens, mints the internal JWT and evaluates access policy.

.cta title:{Ready to start building?}
    Set up the stack, then explore the APIs: [Setting up the environment](../docs/setup/setting-up.qd) · [OpenAPI spec](../docs/reference/api-reference.qd)
